      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "ka, pi and nuk",
      "text": "Ka means \"has\": Ana ka ujë. Put nuk in front of the verb to say no: Sam nuk ka kafe. The verb pi (drink) keeps the same shape for \"I\", \"you\" and \"she or he\": unë pi, ti pi, ai pi.",
